# Gnanova Real Estate AI - Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS (utility-first, mobile-first)
- **Database**: Supabase (PostgreSQL + pgvector)
- **AI**: OpenAI GPT-4o, VAPI (Voice AI)
- **Components**: Custom components with Tailwind (lucide-react icons)

## Project Structure
- `/src/pages/Dashboard/` - Dashboard pages
- `/src/components/` - Reusable components
- `/src/lib/` - Utilities and configs
- `/server/api/` - Backend API routes (Express)
- `/supabase/` - Database migrations and functions

## Coding Standards

### TypeScript
- Use TypeScript for all new files
- Define proper interfaces for all data types
- Use strict type checking
- Export types from separate files when shared

### React
- Use functional components with hooks
- useState, useEffect, custom hooks as needed
- Proper error boundaries
- Loading states for all async operations

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS utility classes only
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Dark mode support (dark: prefix)
- Use lucide-react for icons
- Consistent spacing: p-4, p-6, gap-4, etc.
- Card-based layouts with shadows

### Supabase
- Client setup in `/src/lib/supabase.ts`
- Use Row Level Security (RLS)
- Real-time subscriptions for live data
- Proper error handling for queries
- Type-safe queries with TypeScript

### API Integration
- OpenAI API for embeddings and content generation
- VAPI for voice calls
- Twilio for WhatsApp
- Error handling with try-catch
- Loading states and user feedback

### UI/UX
- Modern, clean, professional design
- Responsive (mobile, tablet, desktop)
- Loading skeletons or spinners
- Toast notifications for actions
- Confirmation modals for destructive actions
- Accessible (ARIA labels, keyboard navigation)

### Database Tables
- `leads` - Lead information
- `properties` - Property listings with embeddings
- `calls` - Call logs and transcripts
- `bookings` / `appointments` - Scheduled viewings
- `agents` - Agent accounts
- `outbound_campaigns` - Campaign data
- `campaign_leads` - Campaign progress

### File Naming
- Components: PascalCase (e.g., `LeadsTable.tsx`)
- Pages: PascalCase (e.g., `Dashboard.tsx`)
- Utils: camelCase (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
- Types: PascalCase (e.g., `Lead.ts`, `Property.ts`)

### Code Organization
- Keep components small and focused
- Extract reusable logic to custom hooks
- Separate API calls into service functions
- Use constants for magic numbers/strings
- Comment complex logic

### Performance
- Lazy load heavy components
- Memoize expensive calculations
- Debounce search/filter inputs
- Paginate large lists
- Optimize images

### Security
- Never expose API keys in client code
- Use environment variables
- Validate all user inputs
- Sanitize data before display
- Use RLS policies in Supabase

## Common Patterns

### Loading State
```tsx
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)
const [data, setData] = useState<Type[]>([])
const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)
```

### Supabase Query
```tsx
const { data, error } = await supabase
  .from('table_name')
  .select('*')
  .order('created_at', { ascending: false })
```

### Error Handling
```tsx
try {
  // operation
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Error:', error)
  setError(error.message)
}
```

### Modal Pattern
```tsx
const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(false)
// Use absolute positioning with backdrop
```

## AI Features
- RAG property search with vector embeddings
- GPT-4 Vision for document parsing
- AI-generated listing content (5 types)
- Voice AI calls with VAPI
- Real-time property recommendations

## Notes
- Always test on mobile viewport
- Keep accessibility in mind
- Follow existing code patterns
- Write clean, readable code
- Document complex logic
